Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Numerical Search for RG-Invariant Maximal 3|1 Entropy Loci", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"58717249-4520-4f75-8413-c74a0c5fb6c6"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook constructs the fully symmetric quartic tensor lambda[i,j,k,l] \
for a user-specified number of flavours N. It computes the maximal 1|3, \
equivalently 3|1, entropy equations R proportional to the identity, then \
imposes a finite Lie-chain approximation to all-order RG invariance. The \
finite order is controlled by maxLieOrder. Increase maxLieOrder to test \
stability.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"78a9801d-f63a-4313-8a78-c27d4e22ec46"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Load the helper code", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f4110daf-2c63-4781-8c9c-ad1e72650aba"],

Cell["\<\
The file n_flavour_rg_invariant_entropy_search.wl contains all function \
definitions. It is heavily commented so each routine can be read \
independently.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c60c044e-4601-4621-b6cc-0f2cb3944a61"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Get", "[", 
  RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", 
     " ", "\"\<n_flavour_rg_invariant_entropy_search.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[72]:=",ExpressionUUID->"53d9e021-1ca6-44d4-af45-f2c3eee1e9a4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. User inputs", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dd459818-ddd4-4360-8104-a548fada1e88"],

Cell["\<\
Set the number of flavours, the numerical residual tolerance, and how many \
Lie derivatives to impose. maxLieOrder = 0 means only T = 0. maxLieOrder = 1 \
means T = L_beta T = 0. Larger values impose stronger approximations to \
all-order RG invariance.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ab0532d-d239-43c7-966a-f79739b0de63"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Nflavours", " ", "=", " ", "4"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"precision", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"10", "^", 
    RowBox[{"-", "3"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"maxLieOrder", " ", "=", " ", "3"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"samples", " ", "=", " ", "200"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"workingPrecision", " ", "=", " ", "40"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9894995050534163`*^9, 3.9894995052795477`*^9}, {
  3.989499980088962*^9, 3.989499980262352*^9}, {3.9895000706059933`*^9, 
  3.989500075329322*^9}, {3.989501952399897*^9, 3.98950197943335*^9}, {
  3.989502667455164*^9, 3.989502673073689*^9}, {3.989506629887927*^9, 
  3.989506631033877*^9}, {3.989506854034945*^9, 3.989506897651928*^9}, {
  3.989506989712049*^9, 3.989506989823256*^9}, {3.9895071302494*^9, 
  3.989507131606318*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[167]:=",ExpressionUUID->"205c175a-d235-487b-ad93-aa99dfe98335"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Build the symmetric quartic model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3387838f-4ba9-423d-b72b-2dae557aa465"],

Cell["\<\
BuildQuarticModel creates one independent variable for each component of a \
completely symmetric lambda[i,j,k,l]. The model also contains a function \
Lambda[i,j,k,l] that automatically sorts the indices and returns the correct \
independent variable.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe44f5dd-b294-4f50-9e1c-69117480257e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"model", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BuildQuarticModel", "[", "Nflavours", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Variables\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[172]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9467cca1-8538-4c37-a024-a717303eaf89"],

